#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:10
msgid "What I do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:12
msgid ""
"Hold the canonical doctrine — and one specific paste-ready sentence — for"
" the **\"multiple related specs\"** condition: when the body of work in "
"front of the user is two or more topically related specs with no shared "
"initiative parent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:17
msgid "Two surfaces consume me:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:19
msgid ""
"**`/roadmap-review`** (interactive triage) — surfaces orphan clusters "
"that already exist in the planning corpus and offers to `/compose` them "
"into an initiative."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:22
msgid ""
"**`/design`** (multi-spec routing, sibling spec `multi-spec-design-"
"routing`) — catches the condition *at design time*, before the second or "
"third related spec lands, and routes the user toward `/compose` first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:27
msgid ""
"Both surfaces quote the same canonical sentence from me. I exist so the "
"wording stays consistent across the two moments and neither surface re-"
"invents it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:31
msgid "Goal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:33
msgid ""
"When two or more related specs would be created (or already exist "
"unparented), prefer **initiative-first composition** — `/compose` into a "
"parent with phased children — over scaffolding N flat sibling features. "
"Flat orphans become discoverable only by accident; an initiative parent "
"makes the work legible as a unit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:39
msgid ""
"This is composition discipline, not sizing. A `medium` cluster of three "
"orphans is a composition problem; the size ladder doesn't model it. "
"That's why this skill exists separately from `spec-sizing`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:43
msgid "Canonical phrasing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:45
msgid "The sentence both surfaces quote verbatim, substituting the slugs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:47
msgid ""
"`<slug-a>`, `<slug-b>`, and `<slug-c>` look topically related and none of"
" them have an initiative parent. If they're one body of work, `/compose` "
"lifts them into a shared initiative. If they're genuinely independent, no"
" action needed. Want me to `/compose` them?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:53
msgid ""
"Do not paraphrase. Quoting keeps the user's mental model of the nudge "
"stable across the design-time and triage-time surfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:56
msgid "Triggers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:58
msgid ""
"The nudge fires when **any** of the following is true during a `/design` "
"invocation. These are deliberately not AND-ed — each one independently "
"signals a composition moment, and a single trigger is enough."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:63
msgid ""
"**Explicit multi-deliverable phrasing.** The `/design` request names ≥ 2 "
"distinct deliverables. Pattern recognition the agent already does — no "
"NLP, no learned model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:66
msgid "*\"design X, Y, and Z\"*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:67
msgid "*\"spec out these three things\"*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:68
msgid "*\"I need specs for A and B\"*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:69
msgid "*\"design these four features\"*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:70
msgid ""
"*\"and also\"* / *\"plus\"* / *\"along with\"* when each side names a "
"discrete deliverable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:73
msgid ""
"**Lead-identified sub-deliverables.** While clarifying the request, the "
"lead recognizes ≥ 2 independent sub-deliverables that would each warrant "
"their own spec — different surfaces, different acceptance criteria, could"
" ship independently. This is design judgment, not a mechanical rule. Lean"
" toward *not* firing if uncertain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:80
msgid ""
"**Rolled-up size ≥ `large`.** If the lead can estimate the deliverables' "
"sizes individually, and the midpoint-sum across them rolls up to `large` "
"or higher on the shared ladder (per the midpoint-sum mechanic in "
"`internal/snapshot/rollup.go`), the cluster wants an initiative parent "
"regardless of how the request was phrased. Fall back to triggers #1 / #2 "
"when there isn't enough information to estimate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:88
msgid "Any-of. One trigger is sufficient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:90
msgid "Phrasing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:92
msgid ""
"Paste-ready text the lead quotes when a trigger fires. Direct, non-"
"hedging — name the alternative and ask. The canonical sentence under `## "
"Canonical phrasing` above is the orphan-cluster variant used by "
"`/roadmap-review`; the variants below are the design-time variants, "
"parameterized by which trigger fired."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:98
msgid "Trigger #1 — request names multiple deliverables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:100
msgid ""
"You named N deliverables here (`<thing-a>`, `<thing-b>`, `<thing-c>`). "
"I'd recommend running `/compose` instead — that creates an initiative "
"with N child stubs, ready for individual `/design` passes when each is "
"up. The alternative is N flat sibling specs with no parent, which usually"
" gets reparented later anyway. Want me to `/compose` this, or proceed "
"with the siblings here?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:108
msgid "Trigger #2 — lead spotted sub-deliverables during clarification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:110
msgid ""
"Listening to this, it sounds like ≥ 2 independent pieces of work "
"(`<piece-a>`, `<piece-b>`) — each could ship on its own and each wants "
"its own acceptance criteria. I'd recommend `/compose` instead — scaffold "
"an initiative parent now and `/design` each child when you're ready to "
"flesh it out. Want to switch, or stay in `/design` and ship this as a "
"single spec?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:117
msgid "Trigger #3 — rolled-up size ≥ `large`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:119
msgid ""
"This is shaping up as ≥ `large` rolled up across multiple deliverables. "
"That's initiative territory — I'd recommend `/compose` instead, which "
"scaffolds the parent and lets you sequence the children. Want to switch, "
"or stay in `/design` and ship this as a single spec?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:125
msgid ""
"Substitute the slugs / deliverable names inline; otherwise quote "
"verbatim. The wording is short and decision-oriented — a fired nudge "
"should be a 5-second yes/no, not a conversation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:129
msgid "Stance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:131
msgid ""
"The recommendation is **advisory**, never a block. Same stance as the "
"sizing nudge in `spec-sizing` (\"user always wins\"), word-for-word on "
"the override behavior:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:135
msgid "The lead surfaces the recommendation **once per `/design` invocation**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:137
msgid ""
"The user can answer *\"no, just do them as siblings\"* / *\"proceed\"* / "
"*\"stay in design\"* / *\"ship it\"* — any clear decline — and the lead "
"resumes the design flow as if the nudge had not fired."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:140
msgid ""
"The lead records the user's choice in the session so the rest of the "
"session does not re-litigate it. **One decline covers the whole session**"
" (see Suppression)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:143
msgid ""
"On *\"yes, compose,\"* the lead hands off cleanly into the existing "
"`/compose` flow with the user's original `/design` request as the "
"initiative input — it does not simulate `/compose` or scaffold flat "
"siblings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:148
msgid ""
"The nudge is **friction with an off-ramp**, not a gate. A loud linter "
"warning, not a build failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:151
msgid "Precedence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:153
msgid ""
"When the **routing nudge** (this skill) and the **sizing nudge** (`spec-"
"sizing`) would both fire on the same `/design` request, the routing nudge"
" fires **first**, and the sizing nudge stands down for that moment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:158
msgid "Concretely:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:160
msgid ""
"Routing nudge: *\"Your request describes ≥ 2 specs — consider `/compose` "
"to scaffold the cluster as an initiative.\"*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:162
msgid ""
"Sizing nudge: *\"This individual spec is `large` / `x-large` / `giant` — "
"consider `/split` or `/compose` for this spec specifically.\"*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:166
msgid ""
"They describe different moments — composition shape vs. individual spec "
"size — but the user shouldn't get both at once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:169
msgid ""
"**If the user accepts routing** and pivots to `/compose`, the sizing "
"nudges resurface naturally inside the per-child `/design` passes as each "
"child is fleshed out. Each child is sized on its own when it lands, so "
"the sizing nudge fires per-child at the natural moment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:174
msgid ""
"**If the user declines routing** and proceeds with N siblings, the sizing"
" nudge fires per-sibling as usual — each sibling is sized when written, "
"and the sizing nudge fires per the schedule in `spec-sizing`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:179
msgid ""
"Either way, the two stances stay consistent (\"user always wins\") and "
"exactly one nudge fires per moment. `spec-sizing` cross-references this "
"precedence rule so the two skills agree."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:183
msgid "Suppression"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:185
msgid ""
"Three suppression rules keep the nudge from re-firing at the wrong "
"moments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:188
msgid ""
"**Already in a `/compose` flow.** If the `/design` invocation was itself "
"launched from `/compose` (e.g., the user is now fleshing out a freshly-"
"scaffolded child stub of an initiative), the composition decision has "
"already been made. Do not fire."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:193
msgid ""
"**User declined earlier in this session.** If the user has already "
"declined the routing nudge in this session (\"no, siblings is fine\" / "
"\"ship as siblings\" / similar) on a prior `/design`, the lead "
"**suppresses re-firing for the rest of the session**. One decline covers "
"the whole session — do not re-litigate on each sibling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:200
msgid ""
"**The sizing nudge would also fire.** Per the Precedence rule above: when"
" both would fire on the same `/design` request, the routing nudge claims "
"the slot first. The sizing nudge stands down for that moment and fires "
"per-child later (either inside the `/compose` child specs, or per-sibling"
" if the user declined routing)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:207
msgid ""
"These three suppressions are inclusive — any one of them stops the nudge."
" The lead does not need to walk all three before deciding to stay quiet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:211
msgid "Cross-skill references"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:213
msgid ""
"**`spec-sizing`** — the size ladder. This skill does not duplicate the "
"per-type bands or the tier definitions; sizing remains the source of "
"truth for \"how big is this.\" Composition discipline is a separate axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-composition/SKILL.md:217
msgid ""
"**`roadmap-review`** — interactive triage that fires the canonical "
"phrasing above when priority-4 findings (orphan clusters) surface."
msgstr ""

